    "result_text": "The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerEmailUnique.java`** \u2014 new pipeline step that reads the request's (already lower-cased) email via `@Val`, and throws `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` if any existing owner's lower-cased email matches. Email is optional, so a null/blank request email is skipped.\n- **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds **409 CONFLICT** with `{\"errors\": [\"email\"]}`.\n- **`...DuplicateOwnerEmailException.yml`** \u2014 escalation wiring for the handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `emailUnique` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline, right after the telephone `unique` check and before `household`, so it runs after email normalization.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
